`recordToOption()` sets `description` directly from `record[descriptionField]` and then renders it as React text; if that field is an object/array this will throw ("Objects are not valid as a React child"). Consider coercing `description` to a string (or omitting non-primitive values) and avoid spreading the full `record` into state unless it’s needed, since it can be large/non-serializable.
```suggestion
  const rawDescription = descriptionField ? record[descriptionField] : undefined;
  const description =
    typeof rawDescription === 'string' ||
    typeof rawDescription === 'number' ||
    typeof rawDescription === 'boolean'
      ? String(rawDescription)
      : undefined;
  return { ...record, value: val, label: String(label), description };
```

The debounce test waits on real timers (`setTimeout(300)`) with a short `waitFor` timeout, which can be flaky/slow in CI. Consider using `vi.useFakeTimers()` + `vi.advanceTimersByTime(300)` (and restoring timers) to make the debounced `$search` assertion deterministic.
```suggestion
            vi.useFakeTimers();
            try {
                mockDataSource.find.mockResolvedValue({ data: [], total: 0 });

                render(<LookupField {...dynamicProps} />);

                await act(async () => {
                    fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /Select/i }));
                });

                // Wait for initial load (promise-based)
                await waitFor(() => {
                    expect(mockDataSource.find).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
                });

                // Type in search
                await act(async () => {
                    fireEvent.change(screen.getByPlaceholderText('Search...'), {
                        target: { value: 'acme' },
                    });
                });

                // Advance debounce timer deterministically
                await act(async () => {
                    vi.advanceTimersByTime(300);
                });

                expect(mockDataSource.find).toHaveBeenCalledWith('customers', {
                    $top: 50,
                    $search: 'acme',
                });
            } finally {
                vi.useRealTimers();
            }
```
